  - id: Viz_16
    viz_guid: 9768713f-06c4-4d85-b85d-20f5443bf5dc
    note_tile:
      html_parsed_string: |-
        <h2>Golden Rules for Chasm Trap Models</h2>
        <br>
        <body>
        <p><strong>✅ DO:</strong></p>
        <ul>
        <li>Use Shared Month for time-based analysis</li>
        <li>Filter by dimensions that exist in BOTH fact tables</li>
        <li>Check your totals against known values</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>❌ DON'T:</strong></p>
        <ul>
        <li>Mix daily columns with monthly forecast</li>
        <li>Filter by Store when forecast is at Category level</li>
        <li>Assume variance calculations are correct without validation</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Key Insight:</strong> If your forecast total looks suspiciously high, you've likely broken the grain alignment!</p>
        </body>
  - id: Viz_17
    viz_guid: e947ce9a-8bea-4345-b71b-9c2ae95b969c
    note_tile:
      html_parsed_string: |-
        <h2>How to Spot Fan-Out Problems</h2>
        <br>
        <body>
        <p><strong>Warning Signs of Data Fan-Out:</strong></p>
        <p>🚨 <strong>Red Flags:</strong></p>
        <ul>
        <li>Forecast values that seem 10x-30x too high</li>
        <li>Same forecast number repeating across rows</li>
        <li>Variance calculations that don't make business sense</li>
        <li>Row counts that explode unexpectedly</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Validation Technique:</strong></p>
        <p>Always compare your query results against a simple aggregation at the correct grain. If the totals don't match, investigate your joins and filters.</p>
        <p><strong>Remember:</strong> The bridge table only works when you respect the grain boundaries it establishes.</p>
        </body>
